MGAVIDEO FUN_0000_0340: reconstruct the MAIN-MENU background render (asm 0x340..0x387).

0340 is the menu/screen background paint, reached engine cae6 -> e714 -> ... -> e3bc -> (*c564)() = 0340.
It (1) copies a 768-byte palette from the screen descriptor's resource segment into the driver palette
buffer word[DGROUP:0x782], (2) RLE-decodes the descriptor's background IMAGE straight into the VGA
framebuffer at 0xA0000, and (3) uploads the palette (FUN_0000_0410).  Ghidra dropped every segment base:

  asm 0x340: mov es,cx ; mov ax,es:[bx]        -> uVar3 = *param_2 = word[descriptor:0] = the resource
                                                  SEGMENT (holds 768B palette at :0, RLE image at :0x300)
  asm 0x34b: mov ds,ax                          -> src segment for both the palette copy and the RLE blit
  asm 0x34d: mov BYTE ss:0x786,0                -> Ghidra wrote DAT_2000_c216 (linear 0x2c216, WRONG ss
                                                  base); real target = byte[DGROUP:0x786]
  asm 0x353: mov es,ss:0x782 ; rep movsw 0x180  -> dst = word[DGROUP:0x782]:0 (palette buffer); Ghidra
                                                  dropped BOTH bases -> the NULL rep-movs that SIGSEGV'd
  asm 0x361: mov es,0xA000; xor di,di; mov cx,0xfa00 ; call FAR [DGROUP:0x336]
             [DGROUP:0x336] = 0xf69:0x57cb (verified from the installed far vector) = the engine RLE
             blitter.  ds:si = descriptor.word0:0x300 (si is 0x300 after the palette copy), es:di =
             0xA000:0, runs until di reaches di+cx = 0xfa00 = 64000 = 320x200.  0x57cb is a MID-function
             entry into FUN_1000_57be, which Ghidra mis-decoded to garbage (in/out/4a2c), so the decoder
             is reconstructed INLINE here from the asm (0x14e5b..0x14e97): PackBits-style RLE -- a signed
             count byte n; n>=0 => copy n+1 literal bytes; n<0 => fill (|n|+1) bytes with the next byte.
  asm 0x379: mov WORD ds:0x780,0x782            -> word store (see patch 092); _DAT_1000_c780 now undef2
  asm 0x37f: mov BYTE ds:0x786,1

The descriptor pointer param_2 is threaded by patch 094 (e3bc sets bx=0xf6cc, cx=ds).  Asm-verified
MGAVIDEO 0x340..0x387 + engine RLE decoder 0xf69:0x57cb.
